This code defines a basic web API for uploading, downloading, and deleting tarballs (tar-gzip archives). The endpoint for uploading is `/upload`, which accepts POST requests with a file attachment. The endpoint for getting a list of files is `/files`, which returns a list of currently uploaded files. The endpoint for downloading a file is `/files/:file_id`, and the endpoint for deleting a file is also `/files/:file_id`. The API utilizes Flask-CORS to handle cross-origin requests, ensuring that the API can be used with web and mobile clients.

This example assumes that you have Flask (`pip install flask`) and Flask-CORS (`pip install flask-cors`) installed. It also assumes you have a directory `/tmp/uploads` to save uploaded files. Feel free to adjust those to your needs.

